<p>The idea, I think, is that 2156's stress and anxiety were strong enough to weaken reality around them, because in my headcanon, that can happen. The numerological significance of 52<sup>2</sup> games of solitaire at a 52% win rate was also enough to weaken reality. Again, in my headcanon, that's also a real thing.</p>
<p>Neither would do anything on their own, though. The fact that 2156 was playing solitaire as a way to cope with her stress connected the two enough to actually crack reality a bit at the intersection of those two forces, enough to create the anomaly. And because 2156 was primarily using it as a way to escape her insomnia, that's how it manifested.</p>
<p>Of course, the real clincher is a bit subtle, because I deliberately chose not to draw too much attention to it.</p>

